<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bergen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bergen is a port city on the west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> and the country's second-largest city. Founded in the 11th century, traditionally by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olaf-iii-of-norway">Olaf Kyrre</a>, it was medieval Norway's chief town and for a time its royal capital. From the 14th century the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League</a> kept a major <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kontor">Kontor</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bryggen">Bryggen</a> on its harbour, controlling the export of stockfish from northern Norway.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bergen.jpg" alt="Bergen" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TomasEE · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bergen_panorama_at_night_-_panoramio_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
